  "id": "COMPOUND:9917 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Osugacestat is implicated in the relationship with M19-MEL through a series of molecular interactions involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1. This enzyme is a target of Osugacestat and is itself targeted by two other compounds: Arillanin A and CDAISMWEOUEBRE-LKPKBOIGSA-N. These targets ultimately lead to the final target M19-MEL. The evidence suggests a potential pathway where Osugacestat modulates the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1, which in turn affects the activity of other compounds, including Arillanin A and CDAISMWEOUEBRE-LKPKBOIGSA-N, ultimately influencing M19-MEL. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between Osugacestat and M19-MEL, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a plausible but not definitive relationship, emphasizing the need for further experimental validation.",
